{
 "name": "Palettes",
 "_about": "THE PALETTES a pattern is coloured from. A pattern names colours by SLOT (0, 1, 2...); a palette says what each slot is, so one pattern is as many colourings as there are palettes that fit it. Slot 0 is the ground unless a pattern says otherwise. The colours are the materials': marbles and sandstones as they are quarried, the glazes of Iznik and Fez, the dyes of carpets, the pigments of a Chinese painted beam, lead, copper and glazed roof tiles. And the DYES of cloth (the fabrics family, four slots each: the dye, a second thread, an accent, a dark): undyed wool and linen, russet (walnut), madder, scarlet (kermes), woad and indigo, weld, green (woad over weld), murrey, black; striped, checked and tartan warps; damask's tone-on-tone with gold; leathers, steel, straw, furs, brass.",
